            <ArticleTitle>Asthma and Respiratory Foundation NZ adult asthma guidelines: a quick reference guide.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>83-102</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The purpose of the Asthma and Respiratory Foundation NZ Adult Asthma Guidelines is to provide simple, practical and evidence-based recommendations for the diagnosis, assessment and management of asthma in adults (aged 16 and over) in a quick reference format. The intended users are health professionals responsible for delivering asthma care in the community and hospital Emergency Department settings, and those responsible for the training of such health professionals.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
